<p>In summary, to extend a U-Net architecture to process videos, we can int=
erleave temporal convolution and temporal attention layers in each downsamp=
ling and upsampling block. These layers allow the U-Net architecture to mod=
el the motion in input videos and generate a sequence of frames that are te=
mporally consistent. To learn more about how these layers can be interleave=
d, refer to [10].</p>
