are:</p>
<ul>
<li>Visual decoder</li>
<li>Temporal super-resolution</li>
</ul>
<h4 id=3D"visual-decoder">Visual decoder</h4>
<p>The LDM generates output in the latent space, not the pixel space. The v=
isual decoder then uses the compression network to convert this latent repr=
esentation back into the pixel space.</p>
<h4 id=3D"temporal-super-resolution">Temporal super-resolution</h4>
<p>This component interpolates between the generated frames, leading to smo=
other motion in videos.</p>
